# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile.field and deploy/Dockerfile.stack (M0-T08).
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight, and the second is the one that matters:
#
#   1. Every excluded byte is a byte not sent to the daemon on each build.
#   2. The context is hashed. Anything in it that changes for reasons unrelated to the image —
#      a docs commit, a local `cargo build`, a git operation — invalidates layers that contain
#      none of it. CI builds these images on every run, and a build that is slow for no visible
#      reason is a build somebody eventually stops running.

# Compiled locally; the image builds its own.
target/

# The image builds the PWA in its own node stage, so the host's node_modules is dead weight and
# the host's dist/ is worse than that: embedding a bundle somebody built on a workstation would
# make the image's contents depend on a machine nobody can inspect. Both are git-ignored anyway.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

.git/

# Not inputs to either image.
docs/
spikes/
.claude/
deploy/.env
